<title>USA: USDA to adjust wheat export Karnal bunt tests.</title>
<headline>USDA to adjust wheat export Karnal bunt tests.</headline>
<dateline>SAN DIEGO 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department will change its procedures to test U.S. wheat exports for the Karnal bunt fungus due to recent findings that the spore of ryegrass smut is similar to the Karnal bunt spore, a USDA official said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Speaking at the annual meeting of the National Grain and Feed Association, Charles Schwalbe, associate deputy administrator for USDA's Plant Protection and Quarantine division, also said the agency is considering relaxing a 14- year-old ban on wheat imports from Mexico.</p>
</text>
